  "verbalization": "Nortriptyline exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c9, as evidenced by multiple paths in the dataset. The core mechanism involves Nortriptyline binding to Cyp2c9, which is then implicated in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, a process mediated by arachidonic acid monooxygenase and epoxygenase activities. These activities are linked to Cyp2c9, suggesting a role in lipid metabolism. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Nortriptyline to Cyp2c9, with consistent scores, indicates a robust, mechanistically supported relationship. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 in oxidative pathways suggests that Nortriptyline may influence lipid metabolism through Cyp2c9, potentially affecting the metabolism of quinones or other substrates. The integration of these pathways highlights a consistent, biologically plausible mechanism by which Nortriptyline could interact with Cyp2c9, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the direct effect on Cyp2c9 activity.",
